⬇️FULL RECIPE⬇️
258 calories 31g protein (for the entire pint, mix-ins included)

Chocolate Covered Strawberry Protein Ice Cream 😋🍦

Original recipe from my Recipe Book

Check out the link in my bio for my Creami Recipe Book with over 150 recipes like this one!

- 1 Strawberry Protein Shake (350-400ml)
- 20-25g Monk Fruit sweetener 
- A pinch of salt
- 1g (¼ tsp) xanthan gum
Mix-ins:
- 1 heaping tablespoon of strawberry jam (I used Low Sugar Smuckers)
- 15g chocolate chips + 2g coconut oil
Right before the Mix-In cycle, combine 15g of chocolate with 2g of coconut oil, melt in the microwave (30 sec intervals, stirring in between), hollow out a hole in the center of the base, and pour in. After spinning on the Mix-In setting, it’ll turn into perfect, creamy chocolate chips. 
258 cal 19g C, 9g F, 31g P

Instructions:
1. Blend all ingredients for the base and freeze (at least 16 hours)
2. Run your pint under hot water for at least 60 seconds
3. Spin on “Lite Ice Cream” setting
4. Spin on “Respin” setting
5. Respin again if powdery
6. Make a hole down to the bottom with a butter knife and fill with the strawberry jam and melted chocolate
7. Run the “Mix-in” cycle

